<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jawaharlal Nehru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1889">1889</a>–<a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Pandit Nehru</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jawaharlal Nehru was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a> in the struggle for independence and a close associate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a>, imprisoned many times by the British. He became the first prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1947 and held office until his death. He shaped the secular, democratic republic of 1950, launched five-year plans for state-led industry, led the Non-Aligned Movement, and suffered defeat in the war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> of 1962.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jawaharlal-nehru.jpg" alt="Jawaharlal Nehru" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harry Pot · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nehru_in_the_Netherlands,_1957.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
